ect that's all you have  so the conversation is really stunted in  the first call or two  he simply recited a prepared statement  for the show and you know as a  journalist that's not really what we're  looking for  you know this well we're not looking to  hear what somebody spent  three weeks drafting or memorizing so  once we got through all of that  we were able to have a real conversation  and i'll leave it up to the listener  whether or not he's truthfully contrite  it is tough to see somebody  who's that young go and be locked up  behind bars  on the other hand it's also hard to  convince  me especially just being around this  quite a bit  that somebody goes behind bars for a  couple of years and is immediately  changed immediately realizes everything  they've done  was wrong and didn't realize it  beforehand and is now somehow a changed  man i remain skeptical  after the break that conversation  continues including whether podcaster  jordan harbinger  thinks convicted fraudster billy  mcfarland is continuing his con  from prison  [Music]  [Music]  we're back now with more of my  discussion with podcaster jordan  harbinger who recently scored an  exclusive interview with admitted frauds  for billy mcfarlane  mcfarland's interview with harbinger is  being licensed and some of the money  will go to compensate the victims  i asked harbinger about the effects the  interview has had  do you suspect he's continuing a con  well right now i don't think it can be  much of a con there's not a whole lot of  con  to be had all he can really do is try to  monetize this experience and this story  and again he doesn't get to keep any of  the money what  one might argue that he gets to remain  relevant in the zeitgeist or in pop  culture  and that could later be monetized  whether that's a con or not  it's hard to say in my opinion it could  even be a continuation of  the previous attempts to get attention  and marketing but he's still got a long  way to go in prison i mean t